file crates/gui/src/graph/input.rs
symbol glide_step
lines 0 21
hash 3c4d8188d4fb1c99
note A glide at the frame's time, from the GlideStep graph_phase sends every frame: the pan moves along an ease-out cubic from the start to the target by the share of GLIDE_TIME elapsed, and lands exactly on it once GLIDE_TIME has passed, when the glide ends. Being time-based, it takes the same time whatever the frame rate; while it is in progress App::frame asks for the next frame at the ANIMATING rate, so it plays out without input. Camera, Pan and Fitted drop it, so the reader's own move always wins.

